<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tapa, Estonia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tapa is a small town in Lääne-Viru County in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a>, a railway junction on the line from Tallinn to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narva">Narva</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tartu">Tartu</a>. It has long been an important military base. Since 2017 it has hosted a British-led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a> multinational battlegroup, deployed after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>'s annexation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a> to strengthen the alliance's presence in the Baltic states.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tapa-estonia.jpg" alt="Tapa, Estonia" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bandaranaice · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tapa,_Estonia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
